      "message": "\u003e \u003e Actually, `shared_pool` might not even require locking if it is embedded in `MEMORY` and a `buddy_system_allocator::Heap` might be enough.\n\u003e \n\u003e What about alloc_shared() and dealloc_shared()? They will need to call shared_pool.alloc() and without shared_pool being a LockedHeap, we can run into concurrency issues potentially?\n\nCallers of alloc_shared() and dealloc_shared() don\u0027t seem to take MEMORY lock and thus we need LockedHeap?",
