      "writtenOn": "2023-04-26T09:16:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Callers of alloc_shared() and dealloc_shared() don\u0027t seem to take MEMORY lock and thus we need LockedHeap?\n\nMy point was that it would be these functions taking the lock on `MEMORY` to access `MEMORY.shared_pool` so that there doesn\u0027t seem to be a need for it to be a `LockedHeap`.\n\n\u003e Can we count on the Heap\u0027s alloc() method being thread-safe? Perhaps the backend implementation of it in toolchain provides for that.\n\n[Yes](https://docs.rs/buddy_system_allocator/latest/src/buddy_system_allocator/lib.rs.html#257-263)",
      "parentUuid": "434d1738_16529e83",
      "range": {
