      "writtenOn": "2023-04-26T15:44:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While testing this, I ran into some locking issue. I *think* we enter fn main() with MEMMORY locked. Later inside that function, while probing PCI devices, we call into alloc_shared(), which does not get the MemoryTracker handle.\n\nMy alloc_shared() changes, which attempted to retrieve the MemoryTracker object from MEMORY hung:\n\n```\npub fn alloc_shared(size: usize) -\u003e hyp::Result\u003cNonNull\u003cu8\u003e\u003e {\n\nMEMORY.lock().as_mut().unwrap().alloc_shared(size);  \n\n}\n\n```\n\nGetting the MemoryTracker handle in alloc_shared() seems messy to me.\n\nDo you have any other suggestions?\n\nI am inclined to go with SHM_ALLOCATOR global variable.",
